        {
          "start": 1512,
          "previous": "| Fin inside products and Except | Ordinary and reviewed C/C++ parameter/result observations cite the original [product reports](native-fin-products-20261007/receipt.json), [Array-of-product reports](native-fin-product-arrays-20261007/receipt.json) and separate [Array dispatch runs](native-fin-product-array-dispatch-20261007/receipt.json). | None for these six C/C++ reports. | VO #1441: execute other native hosts, both Python floors and four Perl ABIs. The later Array runs measure C source and raw-adapter dispatch for `rows`, including first/middle/last invalid positions and recovery. Neither C++ nor `reversed` has independent counters. |\n| Fin nominal fields | Ordinary-source Node JavaScript/TypeScript, including the recorded alias and finite recursive cases. Ordinary and reviewed C/C++ cite the expanded [record reports](native-fin-records-20261007/receipt.json) from `3ece09f`, including Array/List/Option/Prod/Except compositions. C executes 2064 checks and C++ 2053; only C measures dispatch. | None for these two C/C++ reports. | VO #1442: finish other native hosts, both Python floors, four Perl ABIs and browser field acceptance. These nonrecursive, nongeneric native fixtures do not extend npm's recursive coverage to native packages. |\n",
          "current": "| Fin inside products and Except | Ordinary and reviewed C/C++ parameter/result observations cite the original [product reports](native-fin-products-20261007/receipt.json), [Array-of-product reports](native-fin-product-arrays-20261007/receipt.json) and separate [Array dispatch runs](native-fin-product-array-dispatch-20261007/receipt.json). | The [Python/Ruby archive](fin-python-ruby-20261008/receipt.json) retains ordinary/reviewed products and Arrays of products on Python 3.11.16, Python 3.12.14 and Ruby 3.3.12. Each Python product run executes 2038 checks and each Array run 2014; Ruby executes 2039 and 2010. | VO #1441: promote these exact Python/Ruby observations, then execute the remaining native hosts and four Perl ABIs. C measures source and raw-adapter dispatch for `rows`; C++, Python, Ruby and `reversed` do not have independent counters in these reports. |\n| Fin nominal fields | Ordinary-source Node JavaScript/TypeScript, including the recorded alias and finite recursive cases. Ordinary and reviewed C/C++ cite the expanded [record reports](native-fin-records-20261007/receipt.json) from `3ece09f`, including Array/List/Option/Prod/Except compositions. C executes 2064 checks and C++ 2053; only C measures dispatch. | The [Python/Ruby archive](fin-python-ruby-20261008/receipt.json) adds ordinary/reviewed record and variant fields on both Python floors and Ruby 3.3.12, with 2053 checks and all 13 exports per run. | VO #1442: promote only these observed field cells, then finish remaining native hosts, four Perl ABIs and browser field acceptance. These nonrecursive, nongeneric native fixtures do not extend npm's recursive coverage to native packages. |\n"
        },
        {
          "start": 10700,
          "previous": "",
          "current": "The [Python/Ruby archive](fin-python-ruby-20261008/receipt.json) preserves 18 reports from frozen producer `72c5e27`, plus each runtime's original runner, TAP output and queue. All six selected tests per runtime passed without failures or skips. Two independent author roots reproduced the packages, followed by source/build deletion and compiler-free offline installation. Both Python versions produced identical JSON, so the separate execution logs establish which interpreter ran. These local runs used Node 22.23.2 and an explicit glibc minimum of 2.36. Package hashes are retained; the binary archives themselves are not. Dispatch and hosted CI remain unmeasured. The [archive tests](../../tests/fin-python-ruby-evidence.test.mjs) authenticate exact caller bytes, refinement trees, reviewed decisions, package identities and runtime-specific execution records; inventory promotion remains separate.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "start": 17837,
          "previous": "VO #1446 adds checked records through typed, proof-free carriers for C/C++ and npm ABI 8. Each checked input selects a safe constructor over its payload fields; Lean-produced results erase proofs without selecting a constructor. The schemas and independent reviewed source retain erased field names, closed `Nat` indices and per-site constructor choices. [Source checks](../../tests/checked-records.test.mjs) compile generated native/npm Lean and cover normalization, wrong constructors, index mismatches and a standalone result-only package. The ordinary/reviewed/result-only installed harnesses still need execution. No support-table promotion follows from source compilation. Nested checked records, other hosts, recursive and value-dependent runtime payloads remain original #1220 requirements.\n",
          "current": "VO #1446 adds checked records through typed, proof-free carriers for C/C++ and npm ABI 8. Each checked input selects a safe constructor over its payload fields; Lean-produced results erase proofs without selecting a constructor. The schemas and independent reviewed source retain erased field names, closed `Nat` indices and per-site constructor choices. [Source checks](../../tests/checked-records.test.mjs) compile generated native/npm Lean and cover normalization, wrong constructors, index mismatches and a standalone result-only package. Ordinary and reviewed C/C++ installed gates passed at `78a4d3d` with 2020 C checks and 2018 C++ checks each; the standalone result-only gate passed 1001 checks per consumer. npm and strict TypeScript passed all three routes at the same revision: ordinary/reviewed each execute 1011 checks and 1009 rejections; result-only executes 1001 checks. These six original reports await archival and exact support promotion. Nested checked records, other hosts, recursive and value-dependent runtime payloads remain original #1220 requirements.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
